  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1259 AM CDT Thu May 28 2026\n\nCanadian high pressure and an Omega Block pattern will bring a \nlong stretch of mainly dry weather to the region. Right now, only\nsmall precipitation chances are expected with a back door cold \nfront Sunday night into Monday.\n\nTemperatures will average well above normal through much of the \nperiod, with highs mainly in the mid 70s to mid 80s. Right now the\nwarmest day of the upcoming week appears to be Friday when highs\nare expected to soar into the middle to upper 80s. A few 90 degree\nreadings are not out of the question as probabilities are 40-60%\nof hitting 90 or above across northern Wisconsin with a 10-30%\nchance along and west of the Fox Valley.\n\nLow afternoon relative humidity could lead to elevated fire \nweather conditions; however, green-up continues across northern \nWisconsin and pine fuels have become less volatile. Therefore,  \nimpacts may not be as significant as they would have been a couple\nweeks ago.",
